r><![CDATA[GwensBackOnHerBS]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Ada Wong cosplay from Resident Evil 4</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/hqgqfIh</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/NwsMHnR.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>by Felicia Vox</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/3rGqt3r.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>by Felicia Vox</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/5fszmRE.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>by Felicia Vox</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/hqgqfIh</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[FeliciaVox]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>.</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/e6BCe87</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/cJYWkIw.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>$12.99 for a 12 pack of Sprite in North San Diego is wild.

That is basically $1.08 per can before tax or CRV.

And yeah, the digital coupon drops it to $4.99, but only if you buy 5 or more.

That is the part that annoys me.

The “normal” price is insane, then suddenly the store can knock $8 off if you agree to buy a small warehouse worth of soda.

So apparently the real price is somewhere between “reasonable” and “absolutely not,” depending on whether you are willing to stockpile it.

This is why grocery shopping feels like a game now.

Regular price.

Member price.

Digital coupon.

Buy 5.

Mix and match.

Scan the app.

